 you'"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"d like."},{"type":"completed","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"opaque","provider":"anthropic","kind":"thinking","data":{"signature":"","thinking":"","type":"thinking"}},{"type":"text","text":"I couldn't find a verified CAD price for any 27-inch 4K monitor. The shop-price tool mostly returned junk, such as $10 and $45 \"prices\" that are really accessories or monthly payment figures. The Canadian listings I did reach showed no usable price. Here are the models that look worth checking, with US prices from reviews, not Canadian shop prices.\n\n**Best candidates (27\" 4K, typically under about US$400):**\n- **Dell 27 Plus 4K (S2725QS):** Wirecutter's [budget pick](https://www.nytimes.com/wirecutter/reviews/best-4k-monitors). It has an IPS Black panel and 120 Hz. It says a decent budget 4K monitor should cost $400 or less. WIRED's [monitor guide](https://www.wired.com/story/best-monitors) recommends the Dell 27 Plus 4K and says it often sells for under $300, sometimes about $280. The version with a USB hub (S2725QC) is the one to get if you need USB ports. The [Dell Canada page](https://www.dell.com/en-ca/shop/cty/apd/210-BRND) currently says the S2725QS is unavailable. Check Best Buy, Amazon.ca or Canada Computers instead.\n- **Asus ProArt PA279CV:** listed at about [US$366 on PCMag](https://www.pcmag.com/picks/the-best-4k-monitors). It's a 27\" 4K IPS with 100% sRGB, so it suits color-accurate work.\n- **LG UltraGear 27G810A-B:** a 27\" 4K 180 Hz gaming monitor listed at [US$399 on PCMag](https://www.pcmag.com/picks/the-best-4k-monitors). That would likely come out above C$400.\n- **Gigabyte M27U or KTC M27P6:** a [YouTube monitor roundup](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cJvhMpKUb-8) recommends the Gigabyte M27U (27\" 4K 160 Hz) at about $330–380 and the KTC M27P6 (27\" 4K 160 Hz with local dimming) at around $400. I only saw search snippets for these, not the pages themselves.\n\nUS prices usually convert to more than the same number in CAD. Exchange rates and tax mean the Dell and Gigabyte models may land near or under C$400, but the Asus and LG will probably go over unless they're on sale. Before you buy, check the live price on Best Buy, Amazon.ca, Canada Computers or Memory Express.\n\nI can set up a price watch on a specific product page that alerts you when it drops below $400 CAD. Tell me which model and shop you'd like."}]},"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":950,"cache_read_input_tokens":18045,"cache_creation_input_tokens":784},"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","refusal_category":null}]}
